# Local scratch notes
requiremnts1.txt

# Personal data that must never reach a public repo.
#
# The exported application sheet, a resume, or a database dump landing
# in this folder would otherwise be picked up by `git add -A` without
# anyone noticing. Nothing here is a build artefact; these are ignored
# because of what is in them. Use `git add -f` if a genuine fixture
# ever needs one of these extensions.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.sql
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
ace-applications*.csv
*resume*
*Resume*

# The durable memory file stays local, by the user's decision.
#
# It is the one document that records who this is for and what they
# have applied to, and no amount of scrubbing makes that safe to
# publish from a repo owned under a real name. Keeping it out entirely
# is the honest answer rather than editing around the problem.
docs/ACE-KNOWLEDGE.md
